          "evidence_id": "evidence-bcb48c688385",
          "exact": "Despite that bandwidth is a more complicated concept, it is much easier to observe and measure than latency: you can simply execute a long series of independent read or write queries, and the scheduler, having access to them in advance, reorders and overlaps them, hiding their latency and maximizing the total throughput.\nTo measure latency, we need to design an experiment where the CPU can’t cheat by knowing the memory locations we will request in advance."
